	6️⃣ COMMON STEPS FOR TEAM COLLABORATION
	-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

		1. Team Leader creates the GitHub repository        	   → Create the main repository with the initial project files.
		2. Team Leader adds all teammates as Collaborators  	   → Give team members access to the repository.

		3. All teammates clone the repository                      → Each teammate gets a local copy of the project.
		4. [VERY IMPORTANT] Create your own branch           	   → NEVER do your feature development directly on `main`.
		5. Work only on your own branch                      	   → Write and modify code related to your assigned task.
		6. Complete your work and check the changes          	   → Use git status and test your code.
		7. Stage and commit your changes                     	   → git add . and git commit -m "Add login functionality"
		8. Push your branch to GitHub                        	   → git push -u origin <your-branch-name>
		9. Inform your teammates                             	   → Tell the team that your work is complete and your branch is pushed.

		10. Team reviews the changes                               → Review the code/Pull Request before merging it into `main`.
		11. Merge the branch into `main`                     	   → Merge the feature branch into `main` only after the changes are reviewed and approved.


		_____________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________
		-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
		# 1️⃣ On GitHub: Open Pull Request → Review → Approve → Click "Merge pull request"
		# 2️⃣ From command line using `pull`:
				git switch main           → Switch to the `main` branch.
				git pull origin main      → Fetch the latest changes from the remote repository `origin/main` branch and merge (integrate) them into the local `main` branch.
				git merge feature-login   → merge (integrate) the `feature-login` branch into the current `main` branch.
																	
		# 3️⃣ From command line using `fetch`:
				git switch main           → Switch to the `main` branch.
				git fetch origin          → Download the latest commits and remote-tracking information from the remote repository `origin/main`. It does NOT modify the current branch or working files.
				git merge origin/main     → merge (integrate) the latest fetched `origin/main` into the local `main` branch.
				git merge feature-login   → merge (integrate) the `feature-login` branch into the current `main` branch.

		# The key difference between pull and fetch
				git pull origin main      → Fetch + integrate remote main
				git fetch origin          → Fetch only → Updates origin/main → Does NOT change your current branch
				git merge origin/main     → Integrates the fetched remote main into your current branch

		🔥 So remember:
				git fetch  → "Download the latest information from the remote repository, but do not change my current branch."
				git merge  → "merge (integrate) the specified changes into my current branch."
				git pull   → "Fetch the latest changes and merge (integrate) them into my current branch.
		_____________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________
		-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

		12. Push the updated `main`                                → git push origin main (Push the merged `main` branch to GitHub)
		13. Other teammates update their local `main`              → git switch main → git pull origin main (Get the latest merged changes from GitHub)
		14. Continue working on your own branch                    → git switch feature-login (Switch back to your feature branch and continue your work & Create new commits for your next task)
